reading it: `standing` is what the arm costs every session before a question
is asked; `tok/query` is what it delivers per question. `focus` is the share
of the delivered tokens that were the answer, when it arrived at all —
attention is the budget, and everything delivered beyond the answer spends
it. A dump can score recall 1.00 and focus 0.00x on the same run; that pair
of numbers is the difference between present and readable. `noise` is the
share of delivered records that were NOT the answer, counting a miss as
all-noise and an empty return as zero — the one column where declining to
answer scores better than guessing. `obliq` is recall on
questions that never name their subject — the column meaning has to win.
`FP` is the share of questions with no written answer that still got one;
`sep` is how well any confidence threshold could have told those apart
(0.5 = not at all, 1.0 = perfectly). `graph` is the share of questions
whose answer was reachable ONLY through a neighbour — engram-full minus
engram-hybrid is what the edges bought.

